            <ArticleTitle>Adult hydrocoele complicating a lumboperitoneal shunt.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>647-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/02688697.2010.544785</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report an adult patient who developed a right-sided hydrocoele following a lumboperitoneal shunt. While hydrocoeles have been described as a rare complication following ventriculo- and lumboperitoneal shunts in children, we are unaware of any previously reported cases of hydrocoeles resulting from such shunts in adults.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
